{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"33ae652f9199f0781d5d5e5df912695ef1f31e85"},"timestamp":1517356501,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyOTI5ODIyNjU=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2114","origin":"github"},"title":"AutomagicIO: OSError using pandas","message":"#### What is the problem?\nOpening a file with pandas fails with AutoMagicIO enabled. \nError: `OSError: Initializing from file failed`\n\nIn particular, this object fails to initialize in pandas:\n`parsers.TextReader`\nLooks like this is implemented in Cython, FWIW. \n\n#### What steps will reproduce the problem?\nInstall repo, and try to open tsv file with pandas without previous unlocking. \n\n#### What version of DataLad are you using?\nUbuntu 16.04. Latest DataLad from github.\n\n#### Is there anything else that would be useful to know in this context?\nI'm not sure why this was working before (I made a PR regarding this before) and now it fails. I'm guessing Pandas changed how they read files recently. Currently I'm working around this by manually running `datalad unlock` on files I need, but its a bit cumbersome. \n\n#### Have you had any success using DataLad before? (Sometimes we get tired of reading bug reports all day and a lil' positive end note does wonders)\nYep!","files":null}]}